Body:
By capturing the network packets, I think I’ve figured out the exact reason. All that’s needed is to change the baseurl from https://api.ofox.io/gemini, as recommended by Ofox, to https://api.ofox.io/gemini/v1beta/models.

<img width="2855" height="690" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a858348-81b4-44bf-aa8f-7959a37e801e" />

The screenshot was taken using `mitmproxy` packet capture.

Successful requests in the red box were sent from Python code, using the google-genai package.
```python
from google import genai

client = genai.Client(
    api_key="sk-of-xxx",
    http_options={
        "api_version": "v1beta",
        "base_url": "https://api.ofox.io/gemini",
    },
)

for chunk in client.models.generate_content_stream(
    model="google/gemini-3.5-flash",
    contents="hello",
    ):
    print(chunk.text, end="", flush=True)
```


Failed requests came from the OFox service provider configured in OpenCode.
```
❯ cat opencode.json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "provider": {
    "ofox": {
      "models": {
        "google/gemini-3.5-flash": {
          "name": "google/gemini-3.5-flash"
        }
      },
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/google",
      "options": {
        "apiKey": "sk-of-xxx",
        "baseURL": "https://api.ofox.io/gemini"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The path requested by the successful request can be seen through packet capture.
`https://api.ofox.io/gemini/v1beta/models/google/gemini-3.5-flash:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse`
And the path requested by the loser is
`https://api.ofox.io/gemini/google/gemini-3.5-flash:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse`

The `v1beta/models/` path was missing. By manually adding it to the baseURL in opencode.json, this issue could be resolved (the image error has nothing to do with this issue).

<img width="1894" height="935" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3225431-609f-4eb0-a1a1-6d888cacaafb" />

So is the problem on the `opencode` side or the `@ai-sdk/google` side?

@chao23387784  Same. I haven't been able to use `Big Pickle` for 3 days. I think I found out why. Rate limits aren't per user, they're per system. And it seems like system might be overloaded.

> free usage is dynamic, we are always shifting based off what capacity we have vs demand

Source: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/28055#issuecomment-4471949652
